Windows Bazel's hermetic clang toolchain always compiles C++ with the static
release CRT ABI, even in compilation_mode=dbg.  A Debug GN build uses /MTd, so
the C++ objects embedded in the Rust archive otherwise fail to link with
LNK2038 (_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL and RuntimeLibrary).

_DEBUG selects MSVC's static debug CRT and iterator-debug ABI in the headers.
The explicit iterator level documents and pins the ABI expected by /MTd.

Only a Debug build that enables one of Skia's Rust features reaches this code.

diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index df31ad6..d45fd85 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -1373,6 +1373,13 @@ if (is_mac) {
 }
 if (is_debug) {
   bazel_args += [ "--compilation_mode=dbg" ]
+  if (is_win) {
+    # The hermetic clang toolchain defaults to /MT even in Bazel's dbg mode.
+    bazel_args += [
+      "--copt=-D_DEBUG",
+      "--copt=-D_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL=2",
+    ]
+  }
 } else {
   bazel_args += [ "--compilation_mode=opt" ]
 }
